00:26:13,310 --> 00:26:14,510
How are you?" [incomprehensible muttering]

534
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:17,360
They did the whole Hebrew thing. And they pretended I wasn't

535
00:26:17,360 --> 00:26:20,450
there the entire time, and he apologized for them.

536
00:26:20,940 --> 00:26:24,120
To me, he's like, "Don't worry, it'll take some time."
I was like, "I don't need time.

537
00:26:24,130 --> 00:26:24,960
It's okay, I understand."

538
00:26:26,140 --> 00:26:28,480
But I respect the guy. I learned a lot from him.

539
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,270
I learned a lot about what not to believe.

540
00:26:31,340 --> 00:26:31,960
From him.

541
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:35,407
[laughs]

542
00:26:35,540 --> 00:26:36,670
You know?

543
00:26:37,340 --> 00:26:40,820
And you know why I personally believe we should learn from them, additionally,

544
00:26:40,820 --> 00:26:42,530
not just because Allah addresses them.

545
00:26:42,550 --> 00:26:45,260
The fact that Allah addressed them, means that

546
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,260
you know, the way they think about the Quran

547
00:26:47,260 --> 00:26:48,840
is different from how we think about the Quran,

548
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:49,270
isn't it?

549
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:54,020
Now, Allah talks to us in the Quran and Allah also talks to them in the Quran.

550
00:26:54,020 --> 00:26:57,260
But when they hear the Quran, they process it differently.

551
00:26:58,140 --> 00:27:00,270
So I want to understand how they process it,

552
00:27:01,040 --> 00:27:04,960
like what background do they have? What thought process do they have?

553
00:27:04,970 --> 00:27:07,510
So when they hear the aayaat, what is their reaction?

554
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:09,770
I want to see things from their perspective, too.

555
00:27:10,440 --> 00:27:12,450
I just - I think it gives me a different insight.

556
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:14,940
It makes me appreciate things

557
00:27:15,180 --> 00:27:18,350
and I disagree with him on a lot of stuff,

558
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:21,410
a lot from the beginning to end. But it's still fun.

559
00:27:21,730 --> 00:27:22,760
It was a good conversation.

560
00:27:23,630 --> 00:27:26,490
Like, for example, our conversations about Ibrahim (عليه السلام)

561
00:27:26,490 --> 00:27:28,210
Uff.

562
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:31,560
Man. They took Ibrahim (عليه السلام) and they turned him into a different person.

563
00:27:32,740 --> 00:27:34,450
He's not the same Ibrahim that we believe in.

564
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:36,660
It's somebody else they're talking about.

565
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,360
It's crazy. It's just crazy,

566
