but it's fascinating because, you know, for us,

567
00:27:41,900 --> 00:27:44,460
Ibrahim (عليه السلام) is the ultimate example of submission.

568
00:27:46,040 --> 00:27:50,289
إِذۡ قَالَ لَهُۥ رَبُّهُۥۤ أَسۡلِمۡ قَالَ أَسۡلَمۡتُ لِرَبِّ ٱلۡعَـٰلَمِینَ

569
00:27:50,307 --> 00:27:53,620
And for them, Ibrahim (عليه السلام) is the ultimate example

570
00:27:53,620 --> 00:27:55,670
of how you have the right to argue with God,

571
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:57,950
but it's still all good.

572
00:27:57,960 --> 00:28:03,490
So I mean, look, the Quran does not command us, or encourage us, or tell us to hate Jews.

573
00:28:03,500 --> 00:28:07,520
So that's not - you're not a better Muslim because you hate Jews, or whatever.

574
00:28:07,530 --> 00:28:10,670
We don't hate anybody. The Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) didn't hate anybody.

575
00:28:11,340 --> 00:28:14,360
The sunnah of the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) is to have concern for all of humanity.

576
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:21,780
It's the sunnah. If anyone has a right to love and hate, and punish and judge,

577
00:28:21,790 --> 00:28:23,050
it is Allah Himself.

578
00:28:23,060 --> 00:28:26,750
SubhaanAllah Ta'aalaa. Not us. All of us are children of Adam

579
00:28:26,778 --> 00:28:28,400
وَلَقَدۡ كَرَّمۡنَا بَنِیۤ ءَادَمَ

580
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:31,640
"We honored the children of Adam." Which means all children of Adam,

581
00:28:31,650 --> 00:28:34,950
